Ladesäulenregister
------------------

Dataset: chargers (116,443 public charging stations, one point each)

Publisher: the Bundesnetzagentur (Federal Network Agency), its register of
public charging stations ("Ladesäulenregister"), the list as of
1 September 2026.
https://www.bundesnetzagentur.de/DE/Fachthemen/ElektrizitaetundGas/E-Mobilitaet/Ladesaeulenkarte/start.html

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0), as
the register's page states it: "Die Daten sind durch eine Creative
Commons Namensnennung 4.0 International Lizenz lizenziert. [...] Als
Namensnennung für Daten dieser Internetseite ist Bundesnetzagentur.de zu
verwenden."

Credit: Bundesnetzagentur.de.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-12:

  https://www.bundesnetzagentur.de/DE/Fachthemen/ElektrizitaetundGas/E-Mobilitaet/Ladesaeulenkarte/start.html
  (the page, with the licence; 65,761 bytes as read)
  https://data.bundesnetzagentur.de/Bundesnetzagentur/DE/Fachthemen/ElektrizitaetundGas/E-Mobilitaet/Ladesaeulenregister_BNetzA_2026-09-01.csv
  (55,559,083 bytes, SHA-256 cdd8e38f1fa7e8512bd97caa8cf77e9f875436be1f8fe3fe1f2bd9789a504c5b)

Kept: for each station, its id, operator, kind ("Schnellladeeinrichtung"
as Fast, "Normalladeeinrichtung" as Normal), number of charge points,
rated power, the day it went into service, status, street and house
number, postcode, town, county and state as the register writes them,
and its place from the register's latitude and longitude. Left out: the
display name, the parking and payment notes, the opening hours and every
charge point's plug, power, EVSE id and public key. This is a modified
version of the register. The register lists only stations whose
operators completed the agency's reporting, so the stations in service
are more than it holds.


Overture Maps divisions
-----------------------

Dataset: counties (Germany's 399 counties, and Berlin and Hamburg, which
have none of their own, as outlines)

Publisher: the Overture Maps Foundation, its divisions theme
(division_area), release 2026-09-23.1, whose outlines and names here all
come from OpenStreetMap.
https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/

Licence: Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL-1.0), the divisions theme's
licence, as Overture's attribution page states it ("License for theme:
ODbL © OpenStreetMap contributors"). The ODbL applies to this dataset as
a derived database: anyone may use it, and a public derived database
must be offered under the ODbL as well.

Credit: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Overture Maps Foundation.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-12 from Overture's public bucket, the
divisions with country DE, class land and subtype county, and the
regions DE-BE and DE-HH:

  s3://overturemaps-us-west-2/release/2026-09-23.1/theme=divisions/type=division_area/*.parquet

Kept: each division's id, primary name and state code, and its outline
simplified to about 100 m (0.001 degrees, topology kept). Left out:
every other property, among them names in other languages, which
Overture takes for Berlin and Hamburg from Esri Community Maps (CC0).
This is a modified version of the data.


Kontur Population: Germany
--------------------------

Dataset: county_population (the people in each of the 401 counties)

Publisher: Kontur Inc., on the Humanitarian Data Exchange, dataset
"Germany: Population Density for 400m H3 Hexagons", release 2023-11-01.
https://data.humdata.org/dataset/kontur-population-germany

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0), as
the dataset's record on HDX states it ("cc-by").

Credit: Kontur Population, Kontur Inc., via the Humanitarian Data
Exchange.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-12 from the address HDX lists:

  https://geodata-eu-central-1-kontur-public.s3.amazonaws.com/kontur_datasets/kontur_population_DE_20231101.gpkg.gz
  (25,852,962 bytes, SHA-256 b6f2f548e882fe5dd57641473dfae524b77c230698b0e0b1c2b8628a3f3f530f)

Kept: the hexagons' people summed in each county, a hexagon counting in
the county its middle falls in (by the counties' full OpenStreetMap
outlines); 83.3 of the grid's 83.5 million people fall in a county. The
hexagons themselves are not carried. This is a modified version of the
data.


